        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#130710328707508168484707> ;
        skos:definition   "Åland (Finnish: Ahvenanmaa) is an autonomous and demilitarised region of Finland. Åland is situated in an archipelago, called the Åland Islands, at the entrance to the Gulf of Bothnia in the Baltic Sea. It comprises Fasta Åland and about 6,500 skerries and islands to its east. Fasta Åland is separated from the coast of Roslagen in Sweden by 38 km (20+1⁄2 nautical miles) of open water to the west. In the east, the Åland archipelago is contiguous with the Finnish archipelago."@en ;
        skosxl:altLabel   <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#AlandIslands/AlandIslands_en0> ;
