<http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#BodyCorporate>
        rdf:type          <http://example.com/IRD-test-model#Group0> ;
        rdfs:comment      "Should we add the Unit Titles Act 2010 to our list of parliamentary acts?"@en ;
        <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Maori>
                <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#BodyCorporate/rangatopu_en> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition>
                "General - START Help"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "A separate legal entity registered under the Unit Titles Act 2010. Frequently it is set up to administer an own-your-own apartment building with the unit owners being the members of the body corporate. The unit owners pay a levy to the body corporate which is then responsible for the building rates, insurance, exterior maintenance and upkeep of the common areas etc. A body corporate is treated as a company under the ITA 2007 section YA1. A body corporate can delegate some of its duties and powers to a body corporate committee. Some Body Corporates will appoint a director of a professional administrative company to be the Secretary (Executive Office Holder). The director will then delegate access to their staff to complete this work."@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Evidence>
                <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#BodyCorporate/Rangatopu_en> ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "OCTC content; Customer Insight content"@en ;
        sem:guid          "dd554b41-4b7f-4914-9af8-f1d0314fba3b" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/IRD-test-model#Group> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#BodyCorporate/BodyCorporate_en> .

