        skos:definition   "The Cocos Islands are an Australian external territory in the Indian Ocean, consisting of two coral atolls and 27 small islands. Historically known as the Keeling Islands, only two islands are inhabited: West Island, the capital, and Home Island. The islands lie 2,290 miles (3,685 km) west of Darwin, Northern Territory, on the northern Australian coast, and about 560 miles (900 km) southwest of Christmas Island (another external territory of Australia)."@en ;
