        rdf:type          <http://example.com/IRD-test-model#Object-classification> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "<p>Goods, other than capital goods, that are consumed in the manufacturing or sales process but are not part of what is delivered to the customer. In an engineering process, for example, welding rods (which become part of the finished product) are to be treated as trading stock, while welding flux (which does not become part of the finished product) is a consumable aid. <!--EndFragment--><br/><br/><br/></p>"@en , "Goods, other than capital goods, that are consumed in the manufacturing or sales process but are not part of what is delivered to the customer. In an engineering process, for example, welding rods (which become part of the finished product) are to be treated as trading stock, while welding flux (which does not become part of the finished product) is a consumable aid."@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "OCTC content"@en ;
        sem:guid          "af1e865b-52ef-4169-b0c9-475a31522c2f" ;
        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#190233610860084917963353> ;
