        skos:broader      <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Non-individual> ;
        skos:definition   "Council-controlled organisations (CCOs) in New Zealand are entities where a council, or councils, hold significant control, typically through majority voting rights or the ability to appoint most of the directors or trustees. These organizations operate at arm's length from the council, allowing them to manage specific services or assets more independently. CCOs are formed to enhance efficiency, access specialized expertise, and potentially secure funding from sources beyond rates. "@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Council-controlledOrganisation/Council-controlledOrganisation_en> .

