                "IR website glossary"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "Disposal includes: an asset that is compulsorily acquired, an asset taken out of New Zealand (other than only temporarily), changes in use or location of use of a business asset, ceasing intangible asset rights, an asset that is irreparably damaged, any distribution of assets (including distributions of assets to the beneficial owners for no cost), ceasing deemed ownership of a fixture or improvement, or an asset that is lost or stolen if that asset is not recovered in the income year when the loss or theft occurs."@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Evidence>
                <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Disposal/AssetListForWriteOff_en> , <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Disposal/AssetSale_en> , <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Disposal/DisposalOfFMItems_en> , <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Disposal/ExcessEquipment_en> , <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Disposal/FMDisposalProcess_en> , <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Disposal/FMDisposal_en> , <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Disposal/ResidentialLandDisposal_en> , <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Disposal/RetireAnAsset_en> , <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Disposal/RetiredItems_en> , <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Disposal/SurplusAssets_en> ;
