        skos:definition   "At Inland Revenue, EDW is a PAYE tax code used for: Election Day Workers. It applies to people employed on a casual basis to work on voting days (e.g. general elections or referendums). The work must be for voting held in New Zealand. It uses a flat PAYE deduction rate (including ACC earner’s levy)."@en ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Election-day-worker> ;
