        skos:definition   "An Employee Benefit Trust (EBT) is a trust established to hold assets, often shares in the company, for the benefit of employees. EBTs are used in conjunction with employee share schemes and other incentive plans to attract, motivate, and retain employees. They can be particularly useful for the long-term holding of shares, buying shares from employees participating in share schemes, and for allocating shares to key employees. "@en ;
