        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#130710328707508168484707> ;
        skos:definition   "French Polynesia (French: Polynésie française; Tahitian: Pōrīnetia farāni) is an overseas collectivity of France and its sole overseas country. It comprises 121 geographically dispersed islands and atolls stretching over more than 2,000 kilometres (1,200 mi) in the South Pacific Ocean. French Polynesia is divided into five island groups: the Austral Islands; the Gambier Islands; the Marquesas Islands; the Society Islands (comprising the Leeward and Windward Islands); and the Tuamotus."@en ;
        skosxl:altLabel   <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#FrenchPolynesia/PolynesieFrancaise_en> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#FrenchPolynesia/FrenchPolynesia_en> .

