        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#130710328707508168484707> ;
        skos:definition   "Martinique (Martinican Creole: Matinik or Matnik; Kalinago: Madinina or Madiana) is an island in the Lesser Antilles of the West Indies, in the eastern Caribbean Sea. It was previously known as Iguanacaera which translates to 'Iguana Island' in Kari'nja. A part of the French West Indies (Antilles), Martinique is an overseas department and region and a single territorial collectivity of France. One of the Windward Islands, it lies directly north of Saint Lucia, northwest of Barbados and south of Dominica."@en ;
        skosxl:altLabel   <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Martinique/Madiana_en> , <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Martinique/Madinina_en> , <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Martinique/Matinik_en> , <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Martinique/Matnik_en> ;
