        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#130710328707508168484707> ;
        skos:definition   "Mayotte (French: Mayotte, Shimaore: Maore, Kibushi: Maori), officially the Department of Mayotte (French: Département de Mayotte) is an overseas department and region and single territorial collectivity of France. Mayotte is located in the northern part of the Mozambique Channel in the western Indian Ocean off the coast of Southeastern Africa, between the northwestern part of the island of Madagascar and northeastern Mozambique on the continent. Mayotte consists of a main island, Grande-Terre (or Maore), a smaller island, Petite-Terre (or Pamanzi), as well as several islets around these two."@en ;
        skosxl:altLabel   <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Mayotte/DepartementDeMayotte_en> , <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Mayotte/DepartmentOfMayotte_en> ;
