        skos:definition   "Niue is a self-governing island country in free association with New Zealand. It is situated in the South Pacific Ocean and is part of Polynesia. Niue's position is inside a triangle drawn between Tonga, Samoa, and the Cook Islands. It is 2,400 kilometres (1,500 mi) northeast of New Zealand, and 604 kilometres (375 mi) northeast of Tonga. It is 604 kilometers northeast of Tonga. The island is commonly referred to as \"The Rock\", which comes from the traditional name \"Rock of Polynesia\"."@en ;
