        skos:definition   "Non-participating redeemable shares are preference shares that can be called back by the issuing company at a set price after a certain time, entitling holders to a fixed dividend but not a share of the company's surplus profits or assets in liquidation beyond their initial investment and accrued dividends. These shares offer investors a predictable, fixed return and a defined exit strategy through redemption, while limiting their potential earnings to the fixed dividend and their initial investment. "@en ;
