        skos:definition   "The Northern Mariana Islands, officially the Commonwealth of the Northern Mariana Islands (CNMI), is an unincorporated territory and commonwealth of the United States consisting of 14 islands in the northwestern Pacific Ocean. The CNMI includes the 14 northernmost islands in the Mariana Archipelago; the southernmost island, Guam, is a separate U.S. territory. The Northern Mariana Islands are located in the western Pacific Ocean, about 2,400 km south of Japan and north of Guam. They are situated in Micronesia, with the neighbouring U.S. territory of Guam to the south and the Philippines to the west. Japan is to the north."@en ;
