<http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Open-current-MarketValue>
        rdf:type          <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Measurement> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "The open (current) market value is: - the consideration that the goods or services would command between unassociated persons, in similar circumstances, at that time, in New Zealand, or - the value of a \"similar supply\", in New Zealand, between unassociated persons, or - a true assessment of the price of the goods and services, using a method approved by IR."@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "Website glossary"@en ;
        sem:guid          "834048a8-1a51-48ba-8902-3b98f1ccba60" ;
        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#45396487840098489132659> ;
        skosxl:altLabel   <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Open-current-MarketValue/CurrentMarketValue_en> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Open-current-MarketValue/Open-current-MarketValue_en> .

<http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Open-current-MarketValue/CurrentMarketValue_en>
        rdf:type               skosxl:Label ;
        sem:rulebaseBehaviour  sem:RulebaseBehaviourExactPhrase ;
        skosxl:literalForm     "Current market value"@en .

<http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Open-current-MarketValue/Open-current-MarketValue_en>
        rdf:type               skosxl:Label ;
        sem:rulebaseBehaviour  sem:RulebaseBehaviourExactPhrase ;
        skosxl:literalForm     "Open market value"@en .

<http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Opening-value>
        rdf:type          <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Measurement> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "Opening value is: (IV) independent valuation of the market value of the interest at the start of the relevant income year, if you held the interest at the start of the income year; (CA) cost, if acquired in the 2005-06 or 2006-07 income years (only applicable for 2008 income year); (AA) audited set of accounts - the amount that is shown as the net asset value of the interest in audited financial statements of the person for the relevant income year made available to the general public in the relevant income year; (ZO) zero, if acquired in the year, or; (LP) last year plus FIF income. For the second to fourth income years of using the cost method where you have not reset the value by using IV or AA during those years, you can arrive at the opening value by using: the previous year's opening value, and add the previous year's cost method FIF income for that investment."@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "Website glossary"@en ;
        sem:guid          "b47006e0-60cc-49e3-bb94-023aad672b38" ;
        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#45396487840098489132659> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Opening-value/Opening-value_en> .

<http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Opening-value/Opening-value_en>
        rdf:type            skosxl:Label ;
        skosxl:literalForm  "Opening value"@en .

