                "Business definition turned into plain English by CoPilot."@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "A PAYE income payment derived by an employee in  a pay period that is any of the following:  · a payment derived by the employee in the pay period from 1 employer;  · the largest payment derived by the employee in the pay period from 2 or more employers;  · a payment that the employee chooses, where the employee derives payments of the same amount from 2 or more employers  "@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "Business Rules business terms"@en ;
        sem:guid          "39febeac-68a3-4ae7-ab2a-4a83e6b12220" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Employment-income> ;
        skos:definition   "The main PAYE payment for the pay period—either from one employer, the largest from multiple employers, or the one the employee picks if amounts are equal."@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#PrimaryEmploymentEarnings/PrimaryEmploymentEarnings_en> .

