        skos:definition   "A registered postal operator in New Zealand, under the Postal Services Act 1998, is a business that provides postal services like collecting, sorting, and delivering letters, parcels, and other goods. Key obligations include identifying their mail with a unique \"postal identifier,\" keeping records of detained or opened mail for legal reasons, and allowing the Secretary of Business, Innovation & Employment to inspect these records. Registration with the Ministry of Business, Innovation & Employment (MBIE) is mandatory for anyone processing and delivering mail. "@en ;
