        skos:definition   "Retirement village operators, such as Ryman and Summerset in New Zealand, provide housing and lifestyle options for older adults, often with different levels of care, under specific legal frameworks like the Retirement Villages Act 2003. Operators are legally obliged to comply with regulations and codes of practice that cover their responsibilities to residents, including safety, communication, maintenance, and the process for leaving the village. They also manage the financial aspects, which can include setting fees and handling the resale of units. "@en ;
