        skos:definition   "Saint Helena, Ascension and Tristan da Cunha is a British Overseas Territory located in the South Atlantic and consisting of the island of Saint Helena, Ascension Island, and the archipelago of Tristan da Cunha (including Gough Island). Its name was Saint Helena and Dependencies until 1 September 2009. Located in the South Atlantic Ocean, roughly midway between southern Africa and South America. Saint Helena is about 1,200 miles from Africa and 1,800 miles from South America, while Tristan da Cunha is a further 2,700 kilometers southwest of Saint Helena. They are geographically separate from any continent, but often associated with Africa due to historical and political ties. "@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#SaintHelena-AscensionAndTristanDaCunha/SaintHelena-AscensionAndTristanDaCunha_en> .

