        sem:guid          "3726622b-b643-4fc3-bd56-4992880427aa" ;
        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#130710328707508168484707> ;
        skos:definition   "The Collectivity of Saint Martin (French: Collectivité de Saint-Martin), commonly known as simply Saint Martin (Saint-Martin), is an overseas collectivity of France in the West Indies in the Caribbean, on the northern half of the island of Saint Martin, as well as some smaller adjacent islands. The southern, Dutch, half is the constituent country of Sint Maarten, which is part of the Kingdom of the Netherlands. It is located east of Puerto Rico and is north of other Caribbean islands like Guadeloupe. To its north, across the Anguilla Channel, is the British Overseas Territory of Anguilla. To its southeast are the French island of Saint Barthélemy and the Dutch islands of Saba and Sint Eustatius."@en ;
        skosxl:altLabel   <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#SaintMartin/CollectiviteDeSaint-Martin_en> , <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#SaintMartin/CollectivityOfSaintMartin_en> , <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#SaintMartin/Saint-Martin_en> ;
