        sem:guid          "9a406db2-7f7d-4487-8521-84b654bcc81f" ;
        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#188519164724691362719453> ;
        skos:definition   "<p>The Serious Fraud Office is the public service department of New Zealand charged with detecting, investigating and prosecuting financial crimes, including corruption, of a serious and complex nature.<br></p><p>The Serious Fraud Office (SFO) is New Zealand's lead government agency for investigating and prosecuting serious and complex fraud, including bribery and corruption, to protect the country's economic and financial well-being. Established in 1990, it employs a specialized team of lawyers, forensic accountants, and investigators and has the power to require information and documents to conduct its investigations. The SFO also plays a role in preventing financial crime and corruption through strategic partnerships and building counter-fraud capabilities within the public sector.<br></p>"@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#SeriousFraudOffice/SeriousFraudOffice_en> .

