        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "Significant enterprises are all corporate groups or businesses with a turnover greater than $30 million, or with 50 or more employees. In total there are 885 groups that contributed $6.5 billion in tax FY2016. Over two thirds (64.7%) of this group are foreign owned, with Australia being highly influential with 45% based there. Having such a large proportion of these customers based overseas means we are vulnerable to capital moving overseas easily. Significant enterprises can voice their views on tax through the big four tax agents and the Corporate Taxpayer Group."@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "<p>CCS-B content; </p><p><span>People Transition Hub; START</span></p><div><p></p><p>Māori term from Te Taura Whiri Maori Language Commission</p><p></p></div>"@en ;
