        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#130710328707508168484707> ;
        skos:definition   "South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands (SGSSI) is a British Overseas Territory in the southern Atlantic Ocean. It is a remote and inhospitable collection of islands, consisting of South Georgia and a chain of smaller islands known as the South Sandwich Islands. The South Sandwich Islands lie about 700 kilometres (430 mi) southeast of South Georgia. It is located between the South American continent and the Antarctic continent. Its closest neighbours are the Falkland Islands, but even they are a significant distance away. Argentina also claims the territory. "@en ;
