        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#870004799348674954226456202712235> ;
        skos:definition   "State-owned enterprises (SOEs) are government-owned companies established under the State-Owned Enterprises Act 1986, aiming to operate as successful, profitable, and efficient businesses while also being good employers and exhibiting social responsibility. These entities are governed by their own Act but also follow the Companies Act 1993 as they are registered companies. SOEs are responsible to the Minister for State Owned Enterprises and are often former government departments that have been corporatised to manage national assets and deliver services. "@en ;
