        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#130710328707508168484707> ;
        skos:definition   "The United States Virgin Islands, officially the Virgin Islands of the United States, are a group of Caribbean islands and a territory of the United States. The islands are geographically part of the Virgin Islands archipelago and are located in the Leeward Islands of the Lesser Antilles. They do not share a land border with any other country, but they are part of a larger archipelago that includes the British Virgin Islands (BVI), and are geographically close to Puerto Rico. They share a maritime boundary with the British Virgin Islands, and are located east of Puerto Rico, a territory of the United States. "@en ;
