        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "An account held by a customer of a bank, which allows them to deposit and withdraw money with the bank. From an IR perspective, we need to know a customer's bank account number for several purposes: To direct credit any tax refunds to them; To pay them Working for Families fortnightly payments (if entitled); To withdraw direct debit payments from, if the customer has authorised this.  Non-resident and offshore customers must provide evidence of a fully functional bank account when applying for an IRD number."@en ;
