        skos:definition   "A Chief Financial Officer (CFO) is a senior executive who manages the financial actions and health of an organisation. They are responsible for overseeing financial planning, risk management, record-keeping, and financial reporting. Essentially, the CFO is the top financial decision-maker, playing a critical role in the organisation's overall strategy and success."@en ;
