        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "Any enterprise or activity intended to make a profit is classed as a business. If an organisation runs a business, it must pay tax on all profits after expenses (except those made on dealings with its members). However, if a charity runs a business, it may not be liable for income tax on any profits that it uses for charitable purposes within New Zealand. "@en ;
