                "NZ Statistics"@en ;
        sem:guid          "49f2e393-40b6-47dd-a76f-ebe23f3d02be" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PartyAttribute> ;
        skos:definition   "<p>Age is the length of time a person or organisation has existed, measured from birth or legal formation to a given date. Age is a descriptive attribute. It does not create obligations or entitlements by itself, but it is often used to determine whether rules apply (for example, eligibility, thresholds, or responsibilities).</p><p><br></p><p>For a natural person, age is how long they have lived, measured from their date of birth.<br>For a legal entity (such as a company, trust, or partnership), age is how long it has existed as a recognised entity, measured from its date of formation, incorporation, or registration.<br></p>"@en ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#YouthParentPayment> , <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#YouthPayment> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#NewBorn> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Age/Age_en> .

