        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition>
                "Natural_disaster_or_emergency_event_2016-.docx"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "<p>The drought which is causing financial issues for many farmers and growers is likely to affect their income for the 2020, 2021 and future years.  The drought classification has been extended through to 30 November 2021 for the Bay of Plenty Region (Western Bay of Plenty, Tauranga, Rotorua, Whakatāne Districts), Taupō District, Gisborne, Hawke’s Bay Region, Marlborough District, Canterbury Region, Otago Region, and the Chatham Islands.<br/>We have already exercised our discretion to allow late deposits to the income equalisation scheme for the 2020 income, up to 30 June 2021 – no extension to this has been given.<br/>Applications for early refunds from the income equalisation scheme will be allowed.<br/>Customers can request relief from penalties if they have missed filing returns or making payments and may consider re-estimating their provisional tax.<br/><br/></p>"@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "START Help. List of adverse events."@en ;
        sem:guid            "7759b329-bb4c-46ee-b70c-99ed64e647c0" ;
        skos:broader        <http://smartlogic.com/term#134942778228015166252651> ;
