        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#195231629517553071992823> ;
        skos:definition   "Business unit performance indicators (which may also be Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)) are quantifiable metrics used to track and measure the success of a business unit in achieving its objectives. They provide a clear picture of how well a business unit is performing against its goals and targets, allowing for informed decision-making and strategic adjustments. These indicators can be financial, operational, or customer-focused, depending on the business unit's specific goals and priorities."@en ;
