        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition>
                "<p>www.investopedia.com<br/></p><div><p>IR Intranet</p></div>"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "A capital injection is an investment of capital into a company or institution, typically in the form of cash, equity, or debt. Oftentimes, the word injection implies that the company or organization receiving funding may be in financial distress. Can also be capital funding given to the department by the Crown as part of an appropriation."@en ;
