                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition>
                "General - START Help"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "<p>Casual agricultural employee means: a casual agricultural worker, a shearer, or a shearing shed hand. Casual agricultural worker means a person engaged on a day to day basis for a period of no more than 3 months as a casual seasonal worker for the exclusive purpose of doing seasonal: agricultural, horticultural, market gardening, nursery, orchard, tobacco farming work, other seasonal work that, in the opinion of the Commissioner, is work of a like nature to those classes of work. But does not include Agricultural contractors as they are independent contractors, not employees and are subject to tax on schedular payments.<br/><br/></p>"@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "Customer Insight content"@en ;
        sem:guid          "d3afe076-4458-480a-a3a6-6acfb6789af0" ;
