<http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ChangeInitiativeLifecycle>
        rdf:type          <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Methodology> ;
        <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#IsAuthorityObjectOf>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#ChangeManagement> ;
        <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Maori>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ChangeInitiativeLifecycle/EkePanuku_en> ;
        <http://example.com/IRD-test-model#Has-acronym>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ChangeInitiativeLifecycle/CIL_en> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition>
                "<p> </p><p><a href=\"https://irnz.sharepoint.com/sites/kc-initiative-management/SitePages/Initiative-lifecycle.aspx\">https://irnz.sharepoint.com/sites/kc-initiative-management/SitePages/Initiative-lifecycle.aspx</a></p><p> </p>"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "The initiative lifecycle is the construct for how IR manages change initiatives, and starts once an initiative has been prioritised through business planning processes. Having an initiative lifecycle gives us a common language, makes it easier to see what changes are being planned, and provides a “rolled-up” view of what’s happening when for our customers, stakeholders and people.  The lifecycle has four key stages: Emerge, Discover, Design & Deliver (called Deliver for short) and Release. Initiatives follow the same stages although the detailed steps within each stage may vary. The Initiative lifecycle is a subset of IR’s planning and prioritisation process. Before submitting a new initiative to IR's change portfolio, it must be prioritised by the submitter’s business group.  "@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#IAAuthorityProducedBy>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Portfolio> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#IsModelUsedBy>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ProjectPhase> ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Evidence>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ChangeInitiativeLifecycle/ChangeInitiativeLifecycle_en0> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ChangeInitiativeLifecycle/ProjectLifecycle_en> ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "<p>IR intranet; </p><p>Portfolio Office content</p><div><p>Māori term from IR Māori translation register 2021</p></div>"@en ;
        sem:guid          "5bc3d44e-5e49-4192-b455-dc012fb2b83d" ;
        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#143919668998349297872068> ;
        skos:historyNote  "<p> </p><p>Definition and source of definition updated 17 April 2024 to align with the Strategic Portfolio Stewardship definition.</p><p> </p><p>Source of definition</p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:#333333\"><a href=\"http://intranet.ird.govt.nz/portfolio-360/principles-change-initiative-lifecycle\">http://intranet.ird.govt.nz/portfolio-360/principles-change-initiative-lifecycle</a></span></p><p> <br><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:#333333\">The Change Initiative Lifecycle brings together all the business units involved in the creation, design, build and implementation of any initiative. It provides a view of the end-to-end process including all the activities undertaken by the business units, the inputs necessary to carry them out, the outputs resulting from them, and the people involved. The lifecycle is made up of seven phases: Idea, Feasibility, Analyse, Blueprint, Solution Delivery, Deploy, and Review. Each phase has specific deliverables, approval gates with stage gate reports and entry and exit criteria that must be met before an initiative can formally progress to the next phase. These principles accompany and guide the Change Initiative Lifecycle.</span></p>"@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ChangeInitiativeLifecycle/ChangeInitiativeLifecycle_en> .

