        skos:definition   "A \"Closer Economic Partnership\" (CEP) is a free trade agreement between two countries. It aims to reduce or eliminate tariffs and other trade barriers, facilitating the flow of goods, services, and investment between the participating nations. Essentially, a CEP is a type of free trade agreement (FTA) with a focus on deepening economic ties. "@en ;
        skos:historyNote  "It used to be used as a reference to the Australia-New Zealand Closer Economic Partnership at one time."@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#CloserEconomicPartnership/CloserEconomicPartnership_en> .

