                "SD&I content"@en ;
        sem:guid          "d287fed4-81de-42a8-84cf-554af2cd094f" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PlatformAsAService> ;
        skos:definition   "The All-of-Government Common Web Platform (CWP) in New Zealand is a shared web platform, primarily based on Silverstripe CMS, that provides a standardized, secure, and cost-effective solution for government agencies to build and manage their websites. It aims to reduce duplication, promote collaboration, and deliver better, faster, and cheaper services to the public by leveraging shared resources and open-source technologies."@en ;
        skos:historyNote  "Set up in 2017. In 2025 the Common Web Platform (CWP) agreement has expired. All services can now be accessed through the Managed Services Channel Digital Experience Services catalogue on Marketplace."@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#CommonWebPlatform0/CommonWebPlatform_en> .

