        skos:broader      <http://example.com/IRD-test-model#Social-policy-progamme> ;
        skos:definition   "The Commonwealth and Designated Countries Scheme is a reciprocal agreement allowing New Zealand residents to apply for child support via the Family Court when the other parent lives in a participating Commonwealth or \"designated\" country. It facilitates legal maintenance orders and enforcement across borders, with applications processed through the Ministry of Justice."@en ;
