        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#188519164724691362719453> ;
        skos:definition   "​The Commonwealth Association of Tax Administrators (CATA) is an Associated Organisation of the Commonwealth. CATA was established in 1978 by a decision of the Commonwealth Finance Ministers. The organisation helps member countries through conferences, training programs, publications, and knowledge sharing to develop effective tax administrations that promote sustainable development and good governance. Forty-six Commonwealth countries are currently active members of CATA."@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#CommonwealthAssociationOfTaxAdministrators/CommonwealthAssociationOfTaxAdministrators_en> .

