                true ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "Company consolidation allows a group of companies owned by the same shareholders to be treated as a single economic entity for tax purposes. A consolidated group only files only one non-individual income tax return, which includes the income of all the companies in the group. It also simplifies offsetting losses and transferring assets among the companies."@en ;
