        skos:definition   "<p>COVID-19 is a disease caused by a new strain of coronavirus. 'CO' stands for corona, 'V' for Virus and 'D' for disease. Formerly, this disease was referred to as '2019 novel coronavirus&#34; or '2019-nCoV'. COVID-19 has caused a pandemic from late 2019 onwards.<br/>Originally it was known as SARS-CoV-2, as it is similar to the Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome (SARS) corona virus, which also caused an epidemic in 2002-2004.<br/></p>"@en ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#COVID-19Support> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#COVID-19SupportPaymentsScheme> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#HealthAndWellbeingManagement> ;
