        skos:definition   "\"Countering the finance of terrorism\" refers to the legal and practical measures taken to prevent the flow of funds to terrorist groups and activities. It's a key part of the Anti-Money Laundering and Countering Financing of Terrorism (AML/CFT) Act 2009, which aims to protect New Zealand's financial system from being used for illicit purposes. "@en ;
