        skos:broader      <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#IRCustomerResearch> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#CustomerExperienceManagement> ;
        skos:definition   "Customer journey mapping is a visual representation of all the interactions a customer has with a business, product, or service, from initial awareness to post-purchase. It helps businesses understand the customer's perspective, identify pain points, and optimise the overall experience. By mapping these interactions, businesses can gain insights into customer needs, motivations, and behaviours at each stage, ultimately leading to improved customer satisfaction and loyalty. "@en ;
