        skos:broader      <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#CustomerSurvey> ;
        skos:definition   "<p>A customer satisfaction and perceptions survey is a research method used to gauge how satisfied customers are with a product, service, or the overall customer experience, and how they perceive the brand or company behind it. These surveys help businesses understand customer needs, identify areas for improvement, and track changes in customer sentiment over time.&nbsp;</p><p>IR has had these surveys done annually for many years.</p>"@en ;
