        skos:definition   "The Data Quality Assessment Framework (DQAF) provides a structured approach for assessing the quality of data by comparing current practices against best practices. It's a framework developed by the International Monetary Fund (IMF) that focuses on the quality-related features of governance of statistical systems, core statistical processes, and statistical products. The DQAF uses a cascading structure, moving from general to more specific aspects of data quality. "@en ;
