        skos:definition   "Early childhood education is a formal arrangement for the teaching and care of a young child. Early childhood education is provided for babies, toddlers and young children up to the age of 6 years. Licensed and publicly funded early childhood services are the recognised providers of early childhood education in NZ. Early childhood education (ECE) is from birth to school entry age. It is not compulsory."@en ;
