<http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#EvidenceOfIdentityStandard>
        rdf:type            <http://smartlogic.com/class#Method> ;
        <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Abbreviation>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#EvidenceOfIdentityStandard/EOIStandard_en> ;
        <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Is-source-of-rules-for>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#EvidenceOfIdentity> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#HasInterestIn>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PartyAttribute> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#NotNPT>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#EvidenceOfIdentityStandard/ExchangeOfInformation_en> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#EvidenceOfIdentityStandard/ExpressionOfInterest_en> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition0>
                "CoPilot"@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "GES content"@en ;
        sem:guid            "0701db56-5124-46d4-80bf-39495e9f4e53" ;
        skos:broader        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#Standard> ;
        skos:definition     "<p>Documented rules and requirements that specify how evidence of identity is defined, assessed, and applied for a particular purpose.&nbsp;An evidence of identity standard promotes consistency, reliability, and trust in how identity evidence is used. This concentrates on the identity attributes needed and the proof required for those.<br>The standard may set expectations for acceptable forms of evidence, levels of confidence, and assessment criteria, but does not itself constitute evidence.&nbsp;The standard supports decision‑making by ensuring evidence of identity is handled in a uniform and agreed way.<br></p>"@en ;
        skos:editorialNote  "<p>This concept is informed by the former New Zealand Government Evidence of Identity Standard (DIA), which defined evidence‑based confidence in identity.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://docref.digital.govt.nz/nz/identification-management/resource-material-evidence-of-identity-standard/files/002_EOIv2_0-highres.pdf\">002_EOIv2_0-highres.pdf</a></p><p><a href=\"https://docref.digital.govt.nz/nz/identification-management/resource-material-evidence-of-identity-standard/files/002_EOIv2_0-highres.pdf\"></a>​<br></p><p>It has since been superseded by the&nbsp;DIA Identification Management Standards on 1 March 2021. Those standards are focussed on&nbsp;a more modular, risk‑based, and digital‑first standard for authentication and verification rather than evidence of identity.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.digital.govt.nz/standards-and-guidance/identity/identification-management/identification-standards\">Identification Standards | NZ Digital government</a>​</p>"@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel    <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#EvidenceOfIdentityStandard/EvidenceOfIdentityStandard_en> .

<http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#EvidenceOfIdentityStandard/EOIStandard_en>
        rdf:type               skosxl:Label ;
        sem:rulebaseBehaviour  sem:RulebaseBehaviourExactPhrase ;
        skosxl:literalForm     "EOI Standard"@en .

