        skos:broader      <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Meeting> ;
        skos:definition   "A multi-agency meeting is a meeting where different agencies and organisations come together for a common purpose. These meetings can be one-off events or occur regularly. To provide services and deliver effective outcomes, agencies and organisations often need to share information (both verbally and in written form) about individuals. Sharing information enables them to understand and quantify the extent of a problem and then identify appropriate and effective supports, interventions, and services. "@en ;
