        skos:definition   "<p>Within Inland Revenue, financial status is not a subjective label or a social descriptor. It is an evidence‑based assessment used operationally when Inland Revenue determines a customer’s ability to pay outstanding amounts, considers whether recovery action would cause serious financial hardship, and evaluates eligibility for instalment arrangements, remission, or write‑off.<br>IR guidance consistently treats financial status as something that is established from facts, using information such as income, expenses, debt levels, and solvency indicators.<br></p>"@en ;
