        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Vessel> ;
        skos:definition   "In New Zealand, a foreign charter vessel (FCV) refers to a fishing vessel that is owned by a foreign entity but is chartered by a New Zealand company to operate within New Zealand's exclusive economic zone. These vessels can be chartered on either a time or demise basis. Time charters involve chartering both the vessel and crew as a package, with the owner retaining control. Demise charters, also known as bareboat charters, involve chartering only the vessel, with the New Zealand operator taking possession and control, including employing the crew. "@en ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ForeignFishingVessel> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#Charter> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ForeignCharterVessel/ForeignCharterVessel_en> .

