<http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ForeignExchangeGainsAndLosses>
        rdf:type          <http://smartlogic.com/class#Income> ;
        <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Abbreviation>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ForeignExchangeGainsAndLosses/FXGainsAndLosses_en> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "Foreign exchange gains and losses or FX gains and losses is an accounting concept referring to the impact of foreign exchange risk in the financial statements of businesses' monetary assets and liabilities denominated in currencies other than their functional currency. A foreign currency exchange gain or loss is the gain or loss realized due to the change in exchange rates between the booking date and the payment date of a transaction involving an asset or liability denominated in a nonfunctional currency."@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "Tax Technical Website Project"@en ;
        sem:guid          "95afb2fb-d671-4535-a65f-66a915f02dc6" ;
        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#460716479585426992918781858541954> ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#FinancialStatement> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ForeignExchangeGainsAndLosses/ForeignExchangeGainsAndLosses_en> .

