        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "PAS content"@en ;
        sem:guid          "3b4605ed-249c-4602-9c5a-5ec2ef43edf1" ;
        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#198788318597836492471216> ;
        skos:definition   "A Free Trade Agreement (FTA) is a treaty between two or more countries designed to reduce or eliminate trade barriers, such as tariffs, quotas, and other restrictions, on goods and services traded between them. These agreements aim to foster economic growth by facilitating easier and cheaper trade, allowing businesses to focus on their comparative advantages and specialize in what they produce most efficiently. "@en ;
