        skos:definition   "The General Agreement on Trade in Services (GATS) is a World Trade Organization (WTO) treaty that aims to create a predictable and transparent system for international trade in services. It entered into force in 1995 and applies to all WTO member countries and all service sectors, with a few exceptions. The GATS' core principles include most-favored-nation (MFN) treatment, national treatment, and progressive liberalization. "@en ;
