                "Natural_disaster_or_emergency_event_2016-.docx"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "<p>The flooding in the Tairāwhiti Gisborne region may cause financial issues for some customers. This has been classified as a localised event so no “class of case” decision has been made for income equalisation scheme purposes, however customers will still be able to apply on a case-by-case basis. <br/>If customers require relief, then normal process apply, including late filing/payment penalty remission, and debt arrangements or write-offs.<br/><br/></p>"@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "START Help. List of adverse events."@en ;
        sem:guid            "e0c53d6a-17d2-46de-8425-07ab0c82bd36" ;
        skos:broader        <http://smartlogic.com/term#47138497716934256857234> ;
        skos:editorialNote  "Checked in Viva Topics but it wasn't there."@en ;
        skosxl:altLabel     <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#GisborneFloodsNovember2021/FloodingInTheTairawhitiGisborneRegion_en> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel    <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#GisborneFloodsNovember2021/GisborneFloodsNovember2021_en> .

