        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#188519164724691362719453> ;
        skos:definition   "<p>All people in Aotearoa New Zealand have the right to dignity, equality and respect. The Human Rights Commission works to make this a reality.</p><p><br></p><p>The New Zealand Human Rights Commission, officially known as Te Kāhui Tika Tangata, is the national human rights institution for Aotearoa New Zealand. It was established in 1977 to promote and protect human rights, and foster positive relations between individuals and groups in New Zealand society. The Commission works independently of the government but is funded by the Ministry of Justice. </p>"@en ;
