        skos:definition   "IR roles help deliver, operate, enforce, or improve New Zealand’s tax and social policy system. They support New Zealand’s tax and social policy system by helping people, applying the rules fairly, providing expert advice, or designing and improving how the system works. Together, these roles ensure people can meet their obligations, receive the right entitlements, and trust that the system is fair, accurate, and well run."@en ;
