        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#AgentManagement> ;
        skos:definition   "An Individual Quality Review (IQR) is a performance assessment that evaluates the quality of an individual's work against established standards. It's a method to ensure work meets a minimum level of correctness and consistency, often used as part of an overall performance evaluation. IQRs are typically conducted by reviewing a selection of an individual's work products, such as cases or projects, to determine the quality of their performance. "@en ;
