<http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#InformationSecurityOffice>
        rdf:type          <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#IRBusinessGroup> ;
        <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Maori>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#InformationSecurityOffice/TariWhakahaumaruParongo_en> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#InformationSecurityOffice/TiakiParongo_en> ;
        <http://example.com/IRD-test-model#Is-managed-by>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ChiefInformationSecurityOfficer> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#HasInterestIn>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#InformationSecurityManagement> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                true ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition>
                "https://irnz.sharepoint.com/sites/CORP-information-security/SitePages/How-we-make-a-difference.aspx"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "Check out a few of the ways the Information Security Team makes a difference at Inland Revenue: Providing confidence to the ELT, the public, stakeholders, and government officials that we are meeting the Government’s security priorities and are keeping Inland Revenue safe. Facilitating cultural change where security risk is not seen simply as an ICT issue and where there is strong security awareness; turning 5,300 passive users into a team of security champions. Contributing to an organisation-wide shift to consistent risk management through certification and accreditation of critical information assets and publicly facing systems. Engaging with the business at all levels in support of their ICT programmes of work and to be seen as trusted advisors who enable, not as an impediment to progress. Ensuring that IR adopts robust security practices and designs by following sound security architecture and development principles at appropriate times during the change lifecycle. Providing early warning of security vulnerabilities and threats through excellent visibility of our environment and what is happening to it at any time. Communicating IR’s security agenda to IT&C and ensuring that we have the right operating model, and resources, at the right time, with the right experience."@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#ProducesAuthority>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PasswordPolicy> ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Evidence>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#InformationSecurityOffice/TariWhakahaumaruParongo_en0> ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Offers-product-service>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SecurityAwarenessProficiencyAssessment> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#WhakangunguKaitiaki> ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "IR Business Units 19-04-2022 obtained from the Talent & Analytics team. Māori term supplied by the Māhutonga Team 2022."@en ;
        sem:guid          "febe75dc-e1dc-48cc-aa55-e999b82b6870" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Enterprise-IntegrityServices> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#InformationSecurityOffice/InformationSecurityOffice_en> .

