        skos:definition   "An integrated forward agenda is a strategic roadmap outlining future actions and initiatives, often within a specific framework. It integrates various aspects and goals, ensuring a cohesive approach to achieving objectives. This can involve aligning policies, communication strategies, and stakeholder participation to address complex challenges and drive progress. "@en ;
