                "Required for eligibility modelling"@en ;
        sem:guid          "68515638-b7f8-46d6-ab88-3679d547c258" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#JudicialAuthority> ;
        skos:definition   "<p>An international court order is a binding determination or directive issued by a court or tribunal established under international law or under another country’s legal system, whose legal force depends on the jurisdiction of the issuing court and the applicable recognition or enforcement framework.<br>Key elements: These are issued by a foreign national court (for example, a court of another country), or an international court or tribunal (such as the International Court of Justice). Thy are legally binding within the issuing court’s jurisdiction but do not&nbsp;automatically apply in other countries. They may require recognition or registration by a domestic court, or the application of international treaties or agreements before they can&nbsp;be enforced elsewhere.<br></p>"@en ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ChildSupportInternationalSupport> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#HagueConventionOnInternationalRecoveryOfChildSupportAndOtherFormsOfFamilyMaintenance> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#InternationalCourtOrder/InternationalCourtOrder_en> .

