        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#158605830624998366163712> ;
        skos:definition   "A private network inside a company or organisation that generally uses the same kinds of software and protocols that you would find on the public Internet, but that is restricted to internal use. As the Internet has become more popular many of the tools used on the Internet are being used in private networks. For example, many companies have web servers that are available only to employees. It is becoming increasing common for intranets to provide access to the Internet through a secure firewall, further blurring the distinction."@en ;
