        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Hearing> ;
        skos:definition   "A judicial settlement conference is a meeting facilitated by a judge where parties in a legal dispute attempt to negotiate a settlement, either for the entire case or specific issues. It's a formal process, often occurring in chambers, where the judge can assist in negotiations but cannot preside over the trial if a settlement isn't reached, unless all parties agree. The conference is confidential, and anything said during it cannot be used against a party later. "@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#JudicialSettlementConference/JudicialSettlementConference_en> .

