        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PartyAttribute> ;
        skos:definition   "<p>A legal entity is a type of party that has legal standing in its own right. It is a person or organisation that the law treats as its own “legal person”. This means it can:<br>•\tenter into contracts<br>•\town property<br>•\thave rights and responsibilities<br>•\towe tax or receive entitlements<br>•\tbe sued or take legal action in its own name<br>In contrast, some arrangements (like general partnerships) are not separate legal entities, so the individuals involved remain personally responsible for obligations<br><br></p>"@en ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Organisation> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#LegalEntity/LegalEntity_en> .

