        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#Correspondence> ;
        skos:definition   "A letter of intent is a document one party will send to another to detail the terms they wish to contract on. It is a precursor to sending a contract and is not legally binding. It is a good idea to send a letter of intent so your potential contracting party knows what terms you want to contract on."@en ;
