<http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#LumpSumOrder>
        rdf:type          <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#JudicialAuthority0> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "Either a receiving carer or liable parent can apply for a lump sum order when a formula assessment is in place if both: the lump sum application and formula assessment apply to the same parties; one or both parties to the relationship do not want Child Support paid in instalments. Lump sum Child Support is paid in one instalment rather than periodically. It can apply to past and/or future liability. A formula assessment must be in force before a lump sum order can be made."@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "IR knowledgebase"@en ;
        sem:guid          "3787aa59-d257-4d15-ad1b-f80cb9aec2f8" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#ChildSupportCourtDecision> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#LumpSumOrder/LumpSumOrder_en> .

