        skos:definition   "Mainframe as a Service (MFaaS) provides organizations with access to mainframe computing power, software, and services through a subscription model, eliminating the need for upfront hardware investment and infrastructure management. MFaaS vendors handle the facilities, hardware, operating systems, tools, and maintenance, allowing clients to pay a monthly fee for the resources they consume and benefit from the scalability, flexibility, and security of mainframe systems without the associated operational burden."@en ;
