        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#ITManagedServices> ;
        skos:definition   "Managed Security Services (MSS) are third-party services that monitor, manage, and protect a company's digital assets and infrastructure against cyber threats, often operating 24/7 through a Managed Security Service Provider (MSSP). Services include firewall management, intrusion detection, vulnerability management, and incident response, providing a comprehensive security posture that leverages a team of expert security personnel and advanced tools that many companies lack in-house. This allows internal IT teams to focus on other strategic initiatives while ensuring continuous, expert cybersecurity."@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ManagedSecurityServices/ManagedSecurityServices_en> .

