        skos:definition   "Master data management (MDM) is a practice that creates a single, consistent, and accurate \"golden record\" or \"single source of truth\" for an organization's most critical data, such as customer, product, or location information. It involves using technology, tools, and processes to unify disparate data from various systems, ensuring data accuracy, uniformity, and accessibility across the entire enterprise for better decision-making and process efficiency. "@en ;
