        skos:definition   "The Maximum Tolerable Period of Disruption (MTPD) is the longest amount of time an organization's key products or services can be unavailable before the impact becomes unacceptable or causes irreparable harm. It represents the extreme upper bound for how long an organization can tolerate a disruption to its operations before suffering significant damage to its reputation, finances, or ability to function. "@en ;
