        skos:definition   "The NZIER Quarterly Survey of Business Opinion (QSBO) is New Zealand's longest-running and most comprehensive business survey, conducted by the New Zealand Institute of Economic Research (NZIER) since 1961. It polls businesses in manufacturing, construction, services, wholesale, and retail to provide near real-time insights into the economy's current state and to forecast future activity. The survey asks businesses about recent experience and future expectations for aspects like trading, investment, staffing, and costs, serving as a key leading economic indicator for policymakers and businesses. "@en ;
