        skos:broader      <http://example.com/IRD-test-model#New-Zealand-Police> ;
        skos:definition   "The National Organised Crime Group (NOCG) is a specialised unit within the New Zealand Police responsible for combating serious and organised crime, including financial crime. Its primary objective is to disrupt and combat organised crime networks and reduce their harm to communities, working with other government bodies and international partners. The NOCG's efforts are continued within the broader New Zealand Police structure, which includes initiatives like the Organised Crime Intelligence Unit to tackle organised crime."@en ;
