        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#188519164724691362719453> ;
        skos:definition   "The National Tax Agency is the official tax collecting agency of Japan. The NTA was organized in 1949 as an external organization of the Ministry of Finance. The NTA supervises 12 Regional Taxation Bureaus (including the Okinawa Regional Taxation Office, and the same applies hereinafter) and 524 Tax Offices throughout Japan. There is also the National Tax College which trains tax officials, while the National Tax Tribunal serves as a special body engaged in examining requests for review from taxpayers. The Mission of the NTA is “to help taxpayers properly and smoothly fulfill their tax duties.”"@en ;
