        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#188649781203397804479981> ;
        skos:definition   "A \"new\" default member of KiwiSaver is an eligible employee who doesn't choose their own KiwiSaver provider and is automatically assigned to a government-appointed default fund provider. Default KiwiSaver providers are currently BNZ, Booster, BT Funds, Kiwi Wealth, Simplicity, and Smartshares. These members are invested in a balanced fund and are allocated evenly across the default providers. The default providers are selected by the government based on criteria like fees and investment experience and these defaults are reviewed periodically."@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#NewDefaultMember/NewDefaultMember_en> .

