                "General - START Help"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition0>
                "IR website"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "New Zealand foreign trusts (NZFT) are a subset of foreign trusts. A trust is a New Zealand foreign trust if: at all times no settlor of the trust was resident in NZ since the later of 17 December 1987 or the date the trust was first settled, and the trust has a New Zealand resident trustee. NZFTs are required to register with Inland Revenue and disclose information about the trust. NZFTs may also elect to be a complying trust - they are then known as dual-status trusts."@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Evidence>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#NewZealandForeignTrust/NZForeignTrust_en> ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "IR website"@en ;
        sem:guid          "e3740d6d-7145-47f1-857e-46bec77cb3c3" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#ForeignTrust> ;
        skos:definition   "A foreign trust that has a trustee that is resident in New Zealand."@en ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#NewZealandForeignTrustDisclosure> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#NewZealandForeignTrust/NewZealandForeignTrust_en> .

