                "IT & C content"@en ;
        sem:guid          "d7b92751-27f9-4f2e-8dca-e3cce18b37f6" ;
        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#188519164724691362719453> ;
        skos:definition   "The New Zealand Internet Task Force (NZITF) is a non-profit, trust-based organisation focused on improving New Zealand's cybersecurity posture through a community of security professionals from government, academia, and the private sector. It provides a platform for networking, information sharing, and collaboration to counter cyber threats, including working with law enforcement and providing feedback on cyber security legislation. The NZITF also promotes safe practices through workshops and its Coordinated Disclosure guidelines, which help organisations address vulnerabilities and encourage responsible disclosure from security researchers."@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#NewZealandInternetTaskForce/NewZealandInternetTaskForce_en> .

