        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Citizenship> ;
        skos:definition   "<p>Someone who holds a New Zealand resident visa, which gives them permission to live in New Zealand indefinitely, but usually with limits on travel. In everyday terms:&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>You are allowed to live in New Zealand long‑term — there is no end date while you stay in the country.<br>You can work and study in New Zealand without needing another visa.<br>Your visa normally includes travel conditions — you can leave and return only until a specific date unless those conditions are extended or you move to permanent residence.<br>You are not a citizen. Your right to live in New Zealand exists because of a visa, not because you are legally a member of the country.<br></p>"@en ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#NewZealandResident> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#NewZealandResident/NewZealandResident_en> .

