        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#158605830624998366163712> ;
        skos:definition   "Non-production environments are isolated IT settings for developing, testing, and refining software before deployment to the live \"production\" environment, ensuring that real-world operations and sensitive data are not affected by errors or failures. Common non-production environments include development, testing, quality assurance (QA), and staging, each serving specific roles in the software development lifecycle (SDLC). While often perceived as having lower stakes, these environments require robust security measures to prevent data breaches and maintain compliance. "@en ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SystemsDevelopmentLifecycle> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#TestingForum> ;
