        skos:definition     "A relationship status indicating that an individual is not currently in a partnered relationship. An individual is considered not partnered when they do not have an ongoing spousal, civil union, or de facto partnership with another person."@en ;
        skos:editorialNote  "The label Not partnered is based on the current existence of a partnership, rather than on formal legal marital status. An individual who is legally married but separated is considered not partnered for the purposes of this status, because the partnership relationship is no longer in effect, even though the legal marriage has not been formally dissolved."@en ;
