        skos:definition   "<p>A one-off performance payment is a discretionary lump sum paid by an employer to an employee in recognition of exceptional performance or achievement. It is not part of base salary and is generally:<br><br>Non-recurring (paid once, not ongoing).<br>Linked to performance outcomes, project completion, or extraordinary contribution.<br>Separate from contractual entitlements like wages, holiday pay, or redundancy compensation.<br></p>"@en ;
