        skos:definition   "An operational support model is the detailed framework outlining how an organization's people, processes, technology, and governance work together to deliver on its strategy and provide value. It acts as a blueprint, explaining the \"how\" behind delivering value to customers and internal stakeholders by standardizing processes, defining roles and responsibilities, facilitating communication, and ensuring alignment between daily activities and strategic goals. This model helps organizations become more efficient, effective, and adaptable by providing a clear structure for operations and decision-making."@en ;
