        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "Certain applications to the court are made by an originating application. Applications are made by originating application if one of the following statements applies: - They are made under one of the Acts listed under rule 19.2 of the High Court Rules; They are one of the types of proceeding listed under rule 19.3 of the High Court Rules; A direction is sought by one of the office holders listed under rule 19.4 of the High Court Rules; The court allows the proceeding to be filed by originating application under rule 19.5 of the High Court Rules."@en ;
