                true ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "<p>From 1 April 2026, a person transferring their eligible overseas pension fund to certain New Zealand superannuation schemes can elect “scheme pays,” under which the receiving scheme deducts the tax from the transferred amount and pays it to Inland Revenue on the member’s behalf.<br><br>Note: Individuals can still choose to calculate and pay the tax themselves, but the receiving scheme will report the tax to Inland Revenue at the point of transfer.<br></p>"@en ;
