        skos:definition   "Personally Identifiable Information (PII) is any data that can be used to identify, contact, or locate a specific individual, either directly or indirectly when combined with other information. Examples of PII include a person's full name, identity number, email address, home address, and date of birth. PII can be classified as either sensitive (like an identity number) or non-sensitive (like a publicly available name). "@en ;
