        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#188519164724691362719453> ;
        skos:definition   "The Pacific Transnational Crime Coordination Centre (PTCCC) is the operational hub of the Pacific Transnational Crime Network (PTCN), established in 2002 by the Pacific Islands Chiefs of Police (PICP) to combat transnational crime in the Pacific. Located in Samoa, the PTCCC works with 29 Transnational Crime Units (TCUs) across 21 Pacific Island countries to provide a coordinated intelligence and investigative capability against organized crime. It receives support from Australia, New Zealand, and the United States, focusing on efforts to disrupt criminal activity in the region. "@en ;
