        skos:definition   "In New Zealand, there is no strict legal definition of a part-time employee. Generally, it refers to someone who works fewer than 30 hours per week and has a set number of hours agreed upon in their employment agreement. While the exact hours vary, a part-time employee has a regular, ongoing work pattern, unlike a casual employee who works on an \"as needed\" basis. "@en ;
