                "Corporate reporting and planning content"@en ;
        sem:guid          "12ba5ca9-60e9-416f-9471-f60d464065d3" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Enterprise-model> ;
        skos:definition   "A performance improvement framework (PIF) is a structured process or model used by organizations to assess their current capabilities and future needs, with the goal of identifying strengths and areas for development to become more effective and efficient. It provides a methodology to understand the gap between an organization's current state and its desired future state, allowing it to address challenges and implement changes that enhance performance and fitness for purpose. "@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PerformanceImprovementFramework/PerformanceImprovementFramework_en> .

