        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#69007813260322554810672> ;
        skos:definition   "A personal account number is a unique numerical identifier for your bank account, essential for financial transactions like direct deposits and transfers, and can be found on bank statements, void cheques, and by logging into your bank's mobile app or website. While a Primary Account Number (PAN) refers to a debit or credit card number that identifies a specific card and its account, a bank account number identifies the account itself. It is crucial to keep your account number private, as it is sensitive information used in banking transactions, and should be protected with strong security measures to prevent fraud."@en ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PersonalInformation> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PersonalAccountNumber/PersonalAccountNumber_en> .

