        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PartyStatus> ;
        skos:definition   "In New Zealand's health and safety framework, a Person Conducting a Business or Undertaking (PCBU) is any entity that manages health and safety risks, including for-profit businesses and non-profit undertakings like government agencies and schools. PCBUs have a primary duty of care to ensure, so far as is reasonably practicable, the health and safety of their workers and others affected by their operations, which involves eliminating or minimizing risks, consulting with workers, and providing safe working environments and adequate resources. "@en ;
