        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#StageGateReport> ;
        skos:definition   "A Post-Implementation Review (PIR) report is a document that provides a structured evaluation of a completed project, assessing whether it met its objectives, delivered its intended benefits, and stayed within its budget and schedule. It serves as a crucial part of project management, acting as a formal review to determine project success, document what worked well and what didn't, and capture key lessons learned for continuous improvement on future projects. "@en ;
