                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PostIncidentReview/PIR_Memo_INC-_en> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PostIncidentReview/PIR_PBI-_en> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PostIncidentReview/PIRs_en> ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "CI&A content"@en ;
        <http://smartlogic.com/relationship#Has-retention-class_15_Function_40_RDS_18>
                <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#GDA6-1.2.3_Administrative_Planning_and_Reporting> ;
        sem:guid          "18636b72-e8cf-4960-ac24-7629a0aa0483" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#IncidentAndProblemManagement> ;
        skos:definition   "A post-incident review (PIR) is a blameless, collaborative examination of an incident after it has been resolved to understand what happened, why it happened, and how to prevent it from recurring. Key components include a detailed timeline, identifying the root cause, evaluating the response, and creating actionable recommendations for improvement. The goal is to foster a culture of continuous learning and improve processes and security controls to build resilience against future incidents. "@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PostIncidentReview/PostIncidentReview_en> .

