<http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PouHerengaWakaHui>
        rdf:type          <http://smartlogic.com/class#Business-event> ;
        rdfs:comment      "Pou Herenga Waka is both a canoe mooring post - the forum to which our IR leaders will come - and it’s a figurative term for chief or leader. The leader is the pou (mooring) that the people in their teams (each of them a waka) is connected to. From a wellbeing perspective, it is important to have strong, resilient pou for our people to connect to."@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition>
                "<p><a href=\"https://irnz.sharepoint.com/sites/News/SitePages/Pou-Herenga-Waka---People-leaders-hui.aspx\"><u><font color=\"#0066cc\">Pou Herenga Waka - People leaders hui (sharepoint.com)</font></u></a><br/></p>"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "The Pou Herenga Waka hui are for all people leaders, including acting leaders, and are held twice yearly."@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "IR Intranet news. Māori term from IR Māhutonga team"@en ;
        sem:guid          "32e60e60-5757-4324-bf43-9c445167281a" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Hui> ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#TePungaOTeWakaHui> ;
        skosxl:altLabel   <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PouHerengaWakaHui/PeopleLeadersHui_en> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PouHerengaWakaHui/PouHerengaWakaHui_en> .

<http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PouHerengaWakaHui/PeopleLeadersHui_en>
        rdf:type            skosxl:Label ;
        skosxl:literalForm  "People Leaders hui"@en .

