                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition0>
                "Six sigma - SSDSI"@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "CCS: C&O content"@en ;
        sem:guid          "88eafee9-1db4-411c-8074-80507aba46f3" ;
        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#195231629517553071992823> ;
        skos:definition   "Process Quality Indicators focus on assessing a task’s status and progress in comparison with established objectives. According to the Business Process Management (BPM) Common Body Of Knowledge (CBOK), PQIs are vital for measuring results in your business and identifying improvement opportunities.Process quality indicators, also known as Key Performance Indicators (KPIs), are tools that help managers evaluate the quality of processes or the performance of tasks. Companies can also use strategic indicators to measure upper management objectives and encourage continuous improvement. These indicators can help a company better understand which processes deliver value to their customers."@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ProcessQualityIndicator/ProcessQualityIndicator_en> .

