        sem:guid          "8ec1eefa-dcb7-4917-a44b-838415e2a22d" ;
        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#158605830624998366163712> ;
        skos:definition   "In a nutshell, production support is all about keeping live systems and applications working smoothly. Once a piece of software has been built, tested, and released to the public (or to internal teams), it enters what's called the production environment. From that point on, any issues or bugs that pop up are handled by the production support team. For this they will use a specialist production support environment where issues can be isolated and tested without affecting the actual production environment. This can also be named as a Testing Environment. Because of costs, not all systems have a production support environment."@en ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ProblemCaseManagement> , <http://smartlogic.com/term#211882319305457999026722> ;
