        skos:definition   "The Public Benefit Entity (PBE) international accounting standard is a framework for financial reporting by entities that provide goods or services for community or social benefit, rather than a financial return to owners. These standards are primarily based on International Public Sector Accounting Standards (IPSAS), with modifications to suit the local context. "@en ;
