        skos:definition   "A Quality Assurance (QA) Framework is a structured set of processes, tools, and standards used to ensure that a product, service, or organization consistently meets quality standards and objectives throughout its lifecycle. Frameworks define criteria for quality, incorporate quality management practices, and provide a mechanism for monitoring and improving performance. They help in identifying areas for improvement, ensuring alignment with user needs and business goals, and providing formal recognition of quality through various quality marks or certifications."@en ;
