        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Order> ;
        skos:definition   "A recruitment service order (RSO), also known as a Talent Acquisition Services Order (TSO), is a contractual document that confirms an agreement between a client organization and a recruitment provider to deliver specific recruitment services. It outlines the scope of services, including the recruitment objectives and tasks, confirms the terms of the engagement, and serves as a binding agreement before recruitment work begins, ensuring clear understanding and a commitment to the agreed-upon recruitment plan. "@en ;
