                "IR Data Domains and Sub-Domains, v2.5 2021"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "A return is a document that specifies a Party’s position with respect to the obligations and entitlements of an account for a specific period of time.  E.g. IR101 is the return that is completed by a customer to specify their GST position for a period of 1, 2 or 6 months.​ Categorise a table as being in one of the Returns subdomains if the data contains details of collected on a return or any other details about a return (such as filing or error status)​."@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "IR Data Domains and Sub-Domains, 2020"@en ;
        sem:guid          "66c7ec85-0098-4d6e-86e7-763625c6e707" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#DataDomainCategory> ;
        skos:historyNote  "Updated in December 2021 from version 2.5"@en ;
