        skos:definition   "Return on Investment (ROI) is a profitability metric that measures the gain or loss from an investment relative to its cost, typically expressed as a percentage. It's calculated by dividing the net profit from an investment by its total cost and multiplying by 100. ROI helps individuals and businesses evaluate investment performance, compare different opportunities, and make informed decisions by showing how efficiently an investment generates value relative to its initial cost. "@en ;
