        skos:definition   "A sampling specification is a detailed document or statement that outlines a sampling plan, describing the specific criteria and methods for selecting a representative sample from a larger population to draw valid conclusions about that population. It includes what to measure, when and how to measure it, who will perform the sampling, the required sample size, the acceptable level of confidence in the results, and the standards that the samples must meet, ensuring the data collected accurately reflects the larger group and addresses the research or quality control goals. "@en ;
