        skos:broader      <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Government-contract> ;
        skos:definition   "A KiwiSaver scheme provider agreement is a contract between a KiwiSaver scheme provider and IRD that is required for the provider to offer a scheme, use the KiwiSaver trademark, and operate as a manager for KiwiSaver members. This agreement covers matters such as the licensing of the trademark, the operational support requirements, and reporting on member payments and details. It is a prerequisite for the scheme to be registered with the Financial Markets Authority (FMA) and the Companies Office, and allows the provider to manage member contributions and administer the scheme. "@en ;
