                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#SecurityClassification> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "In IR Azure Information Protection (AIP) will require you to classify every document or email before sharing or saving it so it complies with IR’s security classification and labelling policy. This helps us to know what information to retain and for how long. You will be required to classify all documents and emails, including emails that are sent internally or externally. The labelling will place the chosen classification text into the header and footer of your email or document."@en ;
        sem:guid          "2c18f6a5-0662-4ad0-8d4f-068f1789fbe0" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#MetadataValues> ;
        skosxl:altLabel   <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SecurityClassificationVocabulary/SensitivityLabel_en> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SecurityClassificationVocabulary/SecurityClassificationVocabulary_en> .

