<http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SensitiveRevenueInformation>
        rdf:type          <http://smartlogic.com/class#Information> ;
        <http://example.com/IRD-test-model#Has-acronym>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SensitiveRevenueInformation/SRI_en> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition>
                "<p> </p><p><a href=\"https://irnz.sharepoint.com/sites/CORP-corporate-legal/SiteAssets/Forms/AllItems.aspx?id=%2Fsites%2FCORP%2Dcorporate%2Dlegal%2FSiteAssets%2FSitePages%2FHome%2F2022%2DInformation%2D%2DLaw%2Dat%2DInland%2DRevenue%2DFinal%2Epdf&amp;parent=%2Fsites%2FCORP%2Dcorporate%2Dlegal%2FSiteAssets%2FSitePages%2FHome&amp;p=true&amp;ga=1\">Information Law at Inland Revenue</a></p><p> </p>"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "<p> </p><p>Sensitive Revenue Information is a subset of Revenue Information. It means: Revenue Information that identifies, or is reasonable capable of identifying them, (directly or indirectly) or that might reasonably be regarded as private or commercially sensitive information, or the release of which could result in loss, harm or prejudice to the person it relates to. SRI does not include aggregate or statistical data which doesn’t meet the definition above.<br> <br> In regards to SRI, a “person or entity” means that person or entity in their capacity as a taxpayer or social policy customer. For example, an IR policy document that refers to the Commissioner is unlikely to be SRI because the Commissioner is not referred to in their capacity as a taxpayer.</p><p> </p>"@en ;
        sem:guid          "8ceebabe-d83b-4e30-8971-9d9f9676942b" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#LegalInformation> ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SocialPolicyAdministration> , <http://smartlogic.com/term#180994193141146994107004654244499> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SensitiveRevenueInformation/SensitiveRevenueInformation_en> .

<http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SensitiveRevenueInformation/SRI_en>
        rdf:type             skosxl:Label ;
        sem:caseSensitivity  sem:CaseSensitive ;
        sem:stemming         sem:StemmingOff ;
        skosxl:literalForm   "SRI"@en .

