        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#CustomerObligationsAndEntitlements> ;
        skos:definition   "A \"short notice request\" refers to a query that requires a prompt response, often due to its urgent nature or the limited time before a public event, parliamentary sitting, or decision-making deadline. While there isn't a single codified definition, the term implies that the standard reporting or response timelines are insufficient, necessitating expedited preparation and action to meet a critical deadline, as in parliamentary questions or OIA (Official Information Act) requests that affect Ministers. "@en ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Request> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ShortNoticeRequest/ShortNoticeRequest_en> .

