        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Loans0> ;
        skos:definition   "Small business cashflow support scheme account - loan for businesses whose revenue has declined because of an alert level escalation."@en ;
        skos:historyNote  "Started in May 2020 as a response to the COVID-19 pandemic. Applications closed on 31 December 2020. While loans were provided to support businesses affected by COVID-19, the initial application period was only for a few months, although the repayment terms allowed for a five-year period for most borrowers. "@en ;
