        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "A ‘small business’ is any business that is not considered to be a Large enterprise, and generally contains ‘Micro’ and ‘SME’s. They generally have a turnover of under $30m, and can have any number of employees. Younger businesses (new start-ups and ventures in their first 3 years of operating) are more likely to be classed as ‘Micro’, and those operating for longer and perhaps with a higher turnover are more likely to be classed as a Small to medium enterprise (SME)."@en ;
