        skos:definition   "<p>The Social Investment Agency (SIA) was established on 1 July 2024 as a central agency to lead, develop and demonstrate a social investment approach in action. Provide system leadership and oversight of social investment commissioning, and coordinate advice to Social Investment Ministers on commissioning and other related matters. Oversee standards for social investment practice through monitoring and evaluating the performance of social sector investment.<br><br></p>"@en ;
