        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#OperationalServicesInformation> ;
        skos:definition   "A Solution Approval Memorandum is a formal business document used to request and document approval for a proposed solution or action, often within projects or policy-making contexts. It serves as a professional request for official permission, providing a detailed summary of the proposed solution, its benefits, potential drawbacks, associated costs, risks, and timelines. The memorandum is typically addressed to a decision-maker and requires their signature for endorsement, ensuring accountability and formalizing agreement before implementation. "@en ;
