        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#KnowledgeInformation> ;
        skos:definition   "A standard operating procedure (SOP) is a documented, step-by-step guide for completing a routine task or process within an organization. The core purpose of an SOP is to ensure consistency, efficiency, and quality in operations by providing a clear, repeatable \"how-to\" that reduces errors and supports compliance with regulations and internal standards. SOPs serve as crucial tools for training, knowledge preservation, and establishing reliable workflows across departments. "@en ;
