                "http://intranet.ird.govt.nz/sdlc/home"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "This SDLC was used to deliver the IT component of a project at IR. SDLC phase names and activities align with the organisational Change Initiative Lifecycle (CIL). ICT professions use the SDLC templates/artefacts to meet controls designed to safe-guard IR systems. All Run, Improve, Change and External Imperative (R.I.C.E.) are expected to meet controls unless otherwise agreed by the control owner/artefact signatory. ICT professions (e.g. Testing Services, EICT Security) have additional sub-processes which support the new SDLC Control Documents. Those Sub-Processes are detailed under the Sub-Process tab."@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Evidence>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SystemsDevelopmentLifecycle/SystemDeliveryLifecycle_en> ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "Intranet; Portfolio Office content"@en ;
        sem:guid          "13ac0fa9-6c7c-4fcc-aca0-3d5773f1da2b" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ChangeInitiativeLifecycle> ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Non-productionEnvironment> ;
        skosxl:altLabel   <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SystemsDevelopmentLifecycle/SolutionDevelopmentLifecycle1_en> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SystemsDevelopmentLifecycle/SystemsDevelopmentLifecycle_en> .

