<http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#TePungaOTeWakaHui>
        rdf:type          <http://smartlogic.com/class#Business-event> ;
        rdfs:comment      "Te Punga o te Waka means ‘the anchor of the canoe’. It’s used to describe someone who is considered to be an anchor of a family or initiative. In IR’s case, our leaders help to anchor our organisation. Te Punga o te Waka is an ongoing kōrero with these leaders. "@en ;
        <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Has-participant>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SeniorLeadershipTeam> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition>
                "<p><a href=\"https://irnz.sharepoint.com/sites/News/SitePages/Pou-Herenga-Waka---People-leaders-hui.aspx\"><u><font color=\"#0066cc\">Pou Herenga Waka - People leaders hui (sharepoint.com)</font></u></a><br/></p>"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "Te Punga o te Waka sessions provide an opportunity for senior leaders (this includes ELT and all leaders who report to them) in IR to take the time to connect with their colleagues and have the discussions that really matter as they navigate the future for our organisation. This hui is linked to Pou Herenga Waka, our hui for all people leaders."@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "IR Intranet news. Māori term from IR Māhutonga team"@en ;
        sem:guid          "392118e3-9b55-4a6d-8b70-8a9d8a9a719c" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Hui> ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PouHerengaWakaHui> ;
        skosxl:altLabel   <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#TePungaOTeWakaHui/SeniorLeadersHui_en> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#TePungaOTeWakaHui/TePungaOTeWakaHui_en> .

