        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#158605830624998366163712> ;
        skos:definition   "A Virtual Private Network (VPN) is a technology that creates a secure, encrypted connection—a \"tunnel\"—over the public internet to a private server. This process encrypts your data, hides your real IP address, and routes your internet traffic through the VPN server, making your online activity private, secure, and allowing you to bypass geographical content restrictions. VPNs are used by both individuals for security and privacy, and by corporations for secure remote access to internal networks. "@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#VirtualPrivateNetwork/VirtualPrivateNetwork_en> .

