        skos:definition   "Voice biometrics is the science of using an individual's voice to authenticate them. This contactless, software-based technology is highly secure, non-intrusive, and is used in various sectors like call centers and online banking to provide fast and seamless access. By converting a voice into a mathematical template, voice biometrics verifies an individual's identity by matching their live voice sample against their previously enrolled voiceprint.  "@en ;
