        skos:definition   "Electronic workforce management (E-WFM) uses specialized software to automate and streamline tasks like scheduling, time and attendance tracking, payroll, and leave management, aiming to optimize labor costs, improve efficiency, ensure compliance, and provide better visibility into workforce data for strategic decision-making. It helps organizations manage their employees more effectively by reducing manual processes and errors, while offering employees self-service capabilities for tasks such as requesting leave. "@en ;
