        skos:definition   "A case management system is a digital tool that helps organisations organise, track, and manage information related to individual cases, whether in legal, healthcare, social services, or commercial contexts. These systems streamline workflows, facilitate communication, and improve efficiency by centralising data and providing a structured approach to case handling. "@en ;
