        skos:definition   "In New Zealand, a Certificate of Compliance (CoC) is a legal document that confirms a specific activity or building work complies with regulations, such as the District Plan or building consent, without needing further resource consent. It acts as a \"snapshot\" in time, demonstrating compliance on the date the application was received. "@en ;
