        skos:definition   "Debt instruments essentially act as an IOU between the issuer and the purchaser. In exchange for a lump sum payment, the lender guarantees the purchaser full repayment of the investment at a later date. Debt securities - A negotiable or tradable liability or loan. A debt security is a debt instrument that can be bought or sold between two parties and has basic terms defined, such as the notional amount (the amount borrowed), interest rate, and maturity and renewal date. These include government bonds, corporate bonds, certificate of deposits, municipal bonds, or preferred stock. Debt securities can also come in the form of collateralized securities."@en ;
