<http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#DefaultAssessment>
        rdf:type          <http://smartlogic.com/class#Information> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition>
                "General - START Help"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "<p>If a customer must file a tax return and doesn't do so, even after Inland Revenue has requested one, we can issue a default assessment. This is an assessed liability calculated by Inland Revenue to encourage the customer to file the outstanding return. A default assessment is a formal debt owed to Inland Revenue so we will take the same recovery action as for any other debt. The default assessment will be reversed when either of these events occurs: it is determined that the customer is not required to file a return (their policing profile is finalised) or the outstanding return is filed.<br/>Note: If there is a child support liability associated with an income tax default assessment the child support liability may not change even when the return is filed. Refer IRKB page CHI067 Default assessments for child support for more information. If a customer wants to discuss this further transfer the call to child support. If penalties and/or interest have been charged on the default assessment they will be reversed and recalculated on the assessment  once the return is filed.<br/>Default assessments are calculated as follow: from a previous audit, from a previous assessment plus 10% inflation, from a debit amount in IMA, if there is no history from any of the above then a set fall-back figure is used depending on the tax type, entity type, and taxable period.<br/></p>"@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Evidence>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#DefaultAssessment/EDA_en> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#DefaultAssessment/ElectronicDefaultAssessment_en> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#DefaultAssessment/NEDA_en> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#DefaultAssessment/Non-electronicDefaultAssessment_en> ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "<p>D117 Data sources High level; </p><p>Customer Insight content</p>"@en ;
        sem:guid          "451c6090-457e-470c-88ea-3d1eb88e0009" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#CustomerFinancialInformation> ;
        skos:definition   "Assessment completed by IR in the case of non-filing by the customer."@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#DefaultAssessment/DefaultAssessment_en> .

<http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#DefaultAssessment/DefaultAssessment_en>
