        skos:definition   "The Employment Court of New Zealand is a specialist court that deals with employment disputes, primarily those arising under the Employment Relations Act 2000. It has the same standing as the High Court and can hear cases directly or after they have been through the Employment Relations Authority (ERA). The court handles various matters, including challenges to ERA determinations, interpretations of employment law, and disputes concerning industrial action. "@en ;
