        skos:definition   "A fixed-term agreement, also known as a temporary employment agreement, is a type of employment contract that ends on a specific date, when a specific event occurs, or when a specific project is completed. It's a legitimate and versatile way for employers to manage fluctuating workforce needs, like covering parental leave or working on a specific project. "@en ;
