        skos:definition   "The Ministry of Health – Manatū Hauora is New Zealand's lead government agency responsible for the country's health system, providing policy advice, setting direction, and regulating the sector to improve health outcomes for all New Zealanders. It also monitors the performance of other health entities, such as Health New Zealand, which plans and commissions health services. Key functions include advising the government on health funding, monitoring health targets, and supporting public access to health information and services, including the free Healthline service."@en ;
