        skos:broader        <http://smartlogic.com/term#188519164724691362719453> ;
        skos:definition     "Te Puni Kōkiri is New Zealand's principal public sector advisor and leading policy agency on Māori wellbeing and development, focusing on improving Māori outcomes and supporting the Crown-Māori relationship. Established in 1992, its key functions include leading and influencing government policy, assisting the government in its relationships with Māori, and partnering with Māori and private sector entities to achieve strategic investment in initiatives that lift overall quality of life for Māori. The agency's vision is that of Thriving Whānau, believing that when whānau prosper, hapū, iwi, and all of New Zealand will also flourish. "@en ;
        skos:editorialNote  "Do NOT use acronym. Acronyms are not part of Māori customary use."@en ;
