        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#188519164724691362719453> ;
        skos:definition   "The New Zealand Security Intelligence Service (NZSIS) is New Zealand's domestic security agency, responsible for identifying, investigating, and mitigating threats to national security, including foreign interference, espionage, and terrorism. It provides decision-makers with intelligence and advice on national security and offers protective security services and guidance to government agencies. The NZSIS focuses on keeping New Zealanders safe and secure by providing advice on national security, protecting New Zealand's interests and economy, and cooperating with other government and international partners."@en ;
