        sem:guid          "3f2ef6af-b28a-4012-a778-169cd2f4a6bf" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ICTServiceDesign> ;
        skos:definition   "Solution architecture design is the process of creating a detailed blueprint for a technological solution that addresses a specific business problem, integrating various components like software, hardware, and processes into a cohesive system. It involves analyzing business and technical requirements, ensuring the solution aligns with Enterprise Architecture, considering stakeholders, and creating plans for implementation, scalability, security, and cost-effectiveness. The outcome is a comprehensive plan, often in the form of diagrams or models, that guides development teams and reduces project risk."@en ;
