        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "Frameworks, Standards and Charters define ‘WHAT’ we are going to do. Standards define the design norms based on accepted principles, the rules that govern business processes, and/or the minimum operating requirements in a prescriptive manner. Standards are determined by management directives, or external requirements (legislation / regulation or Government request). Standards state the rules governing the implementation of business process - what must happen to meet minimum operating requirements. Standards may also require you to identify what is out of scope or legally permissible exclusions."@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#IAAuthorityProducedBy>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#InternationalOrganizationForStandardization> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#InternationalPublicSectorAccountingStandardsBoard> ;
