        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#TaxPolicyInformation> ;
        skos:definition   "​If any policy changes need to be made to a bill after it has been through the policy and legislative Cabinet committee stages and been introduced, this is usually done through a Supplementary Order Paper (SOP). An SOP that serves a mechanical purpose (eg to break up a bill after its select committee stage) or that promotes minor technical improvements does not need to go through the Cabinet processes)."@en ;
