                true ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "Wine equalisation tax (WET) is levied in Australia for sales of wine including wine exported from New Zealand. If you're exporting wine you have produced to Australia, you may be entitled to a WET rebate. To claim the rebate you must have an excise identification number and be an approved New Zealand participant. i.e. A value-based tax paid on certain dealings with wine sold in Australia."@en ;
