<http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Amusement-Tax-Act-1952>
        rdf:type          <http://smartlogic.com/class#Law> ;
        <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Is-source-of-rules-for>
                <http://smartlogic.com/term#18409388322651895829511> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#HasType>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#LegislationAdministeredByInlandRevenue> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PrincipalAct> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                true ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#LastReviewedDate>
                "2022-05-23"^^xsd:date ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition0>
                "https://stax.ird.govt.nz/wcc/faces/wccdoc?dDocName=IRDOC18829990&dID=18926184"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#IsAdministeredBy>
                <http://smartlogic.com/term#733873855465831453299914748155375> ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Is-amended-by>
                <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Amusement-Tax-Amendment-Act-1963> ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "https://www.legislation.govt.nz/"@en ;
        sem:guid          "5f5e1d48-53b9-42ee-9323-48b6e8576de1" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#_SupersededActsOfParliament-> ;
        skos:definition   "No longer valid. Abolished from 14 June 1965."@en ;
        skos:historyNote  "<p>1. Amusement tax was first imposed by the Finance Act 1917 as a wartime measure. It then applied to all admissions over 6d, and there were exemptions for entertainments devoted to charitable, philanthropic, or educational purposes. In 1918, agricultural and pastoral shows were exempted, and the previous exemptions were clarified by the Finance Act of that year.<br/>2. The rates were varied to some extent by the Finance Act 1921 (No 2) and the Amusement Tax Act 1922 and amendments in 1923 and 1924. The rates of tax introduced by the Finance Act 1930 applied to charges exceeding 1s 6d and were:<br/>1s 6d to 2s 3d<br/>2s to 3s 4d<br/>3s to 3s 6d 5d<br/>Over 3s 6d 1d for every 1s or part of 1s, plus 2d<br/>3. The Amusement Tax Act 1952 consolidated and amended the 1922 Act and the various intervening amendments. New exemptions were provided for entertainments conducted by societies and institutions not established for profit.<br/>4. The Amusement Tax Act 1955 introduced new rates of tax on admissions and introduced an exemption for school concerts even though there was a paid producer.<br/>5. The Amusement Tax Act 1960 abolished tax in respect of all entertainments except:<br/>(a) Horse race meetings.<br/>(b) Cinematograph films, which were not merely illustrative of a lecture or talk.<br/>6. The Amusement Tax Amendment Act 1963 raised the exemption in respect of admission to cinematograph films and no tax was payable if the admission charge did not exceed 3s 11d.<br/>7. With the passing of the Finance Act 1965 payment of amusement tax was abolished from 14 June 1965.<br/></p>"@en ;
        skosxl:altLabel   <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Amusement-Tax-Act-1952/AmusementTaxAct1952_en> , <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Amusement-Tax-Act-1952/AmusementTaxAct_en0> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Amusement-Tax-Act-1952/Amusement-Tax-Act-1952_en> .

