        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ComplianceInformation> ;
        skos:definition   "A restructured debt deed (or similar term, such as a Deed of Company Arrangement or Creditor Compromise) is a formal, legally binding agreement that modifies a debtor's existing financial obligations to make them more manageable, often to avoid default or bankruptcy. It provides a framework for a company with financial difficulties to propose a new payment plan to its creditors, potentially involving extended payment terms, reduced amounts (a \"haircut\"), or other concessions. If a majority of creditors agree to the proposal, all creditors are bound to the terms, allowing the company to continue operating while resolving its financial issues. "@en ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#DebtRestructuring> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#CustomerFinancialInformation> , <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Deed-of-Company-Arrangement> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Restructured-Debt-Deed/Restructured-Debt-Deed_en> .

