<http://smartlogic.com/term#102867796443569056801727>
        rdf:type          <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#PartyAttribute0> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#LastReviewedDate>
                "2026-03-27"^^xsd:date ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition>
                "General - START Help"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition0>
                "Website glossary"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "<p>Net income means total income from all sources less any allowable deductions or current year losses (from self-employment and/or business, a partnership, or a look-through company, but not including any losses brought forward/carried back). As well as salary/wages, self employed income, business income etc, net income includes: Paid parental leave; Weekly Income Compensation and Weekly Compensation from Veterans’ Affairs New Zealand (VANZ); Portfolio investment entity (PIE) income - but only if it was not taxed at the correct prescribed investor rate, requiring you to include the income in your tax return; Interest and dividends.<br/>Net income does not include: Child support received; Portfolio investment entity (PIE) income that is taxed at the correct prescribed investor rate (and therefore not included in your tax return); Employer contributions to your KiwiSaver. If your only income is from your salary or wages (and you don't have any allowable expenses i.e. income protection insurance) your net income will be your annual salary or wages before tax.<br/>See START Help: Independent earner tax credit. </p>"@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "Website glossary"@en ;
        sem:guid          "44fbf2ae-b019-546e-8d68-793486aebc54" ;
        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#887723003806157097850899243914306> ;
        skos:definition   "Net income means your total income from all sources less any allowable deductions or current year losses (including LAQC and LTC losses, but not including any losses brought forward). If your only income is from your salary or wages (and you don't have any allowable expenses, for example income protection insurance) your net income will be your annual salary or wages before tax."@en ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Adjusted-taxable-income> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#ClassNetIncome> ;
        skosxl:altLabel   <http://smartlogic.com/term#102867796443569056801727/AssessableNetIncome_en> , <http://smartlogic.com/term#102867796443569056801727/Net-earnings_en> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://smartlogic.com/label#102867796443569056801727_English> .

