                <http://smartlogic.com/term#357780841536615300976257648179830> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition>
                "General - START Help"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition0>
                "Concept Model Glossary"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfLegalDefinition>
                "​Defined in the Income Tax Act 2007, Section CX2 for the purposes of the FBT rules. "@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#usedAsIRTopic>
                true ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "From the Fringe Benefit Tax Guide (IR409) page 5: Most benefits given to employees other than their salary or wages are fringe benefits. There are four main groups of taxable fringe benefits: motor vehicles available for private use; free, subsidised or discounted goods and services; low-interest loans; employer contributions to sick, accident or death benefit funds, superannuation schemes, and specified insurance policies. If these benefits are enjoyed or received by employees as a result of their employment the benefits are liable for FBT. This could be in a past, present or future job. Employers pay tax on benefits provided to employees or shareholder-employees, even if the benefits are provided through another person."@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "Concept Model Glossary"@en ;
        sem:guid          "a537edb9-58ef-5142-8d33-95cb819f4f87" ;
        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#460716479585426992918781858541954> ;
        skos:definition   "A non-cash benefit that is provided by an employer to an employee in connection with their employment."@en ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Employee-benefit-trust> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://smartlogic.com/label#149875302260300491260325_English> .

