        skos:definition   "The New Zealand Law Society (NZLS) is the national regulatory and representative body for lawyers in New Zealand, established in 1869. Its primary roles are to regulate the practice of law, ensure lawyers maintain high standards through the Lawyers and Conveyancers Act 2006 and rules of professional conduct, and protect the public who use legal services. The Law Society also promotes law reform, upholds the rule of law, and serves its members by offering support, professional development, and representing their interests through a network of branches nationwide. "@en ;
