        skos:definition   "General Disposal Authorities (GDAs) are legal instruments that authorize the disposal of specific types of public records. These authorities are developed by Archives New Zealand and approved by the Chief Archivist. They outline which records can be disposed of and how, ensuring that public records are managed appropriately. "@en ;
