        skos:definition   "<p><!--StartFragment--><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);text-align: left;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);float: none;\">&#34;Subdividing&#34; is where land is divided and separate legal title is established for each of the new sections that are created. A separate title is established by Land Information New Zealand, after receiving an application and a subdivision plan. Whether the activity of land subdivision itself or the sale of subdivided land, there may be income tax or GST implications.</span><!--EndFragment--><br/></p>"@en ;
