        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#UsedInSemantics>
                true ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "Resident withholding tax (RWT) is a tax that is deducted from investment income before the investor receives it. It was introduced for two reasons: So people who receive investment income don't have to pay all the tax in a lump sum at the end of the year; and So people who don't declare their investment income still have tax deducted from it. (Inland Revenue still follows up on undeclared investment income and takes action against people who don't declare it)."@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Evidence>
                <http://smartlogic.com/term#189914628277239459745975/ResidentWitholdingTaxDeducted_en> , <http://smartlogic.com/term#189914628277239459745975/TakeMoNgaHuamoniMeNgaPanga_en0> ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "Website glossary; Business Rules glossary; IR website; PAS content"@en ;
