        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition>
                "<p><span lang=\"mi-NZ\"><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\"><a href=\"https://irnz.sharepoint.com/sites/kc-tax-law-community/SitePages/TLC%20expertise.aspx\">https://irnz.sharepoint.com/sites/kc-tax-law-community/SitePages/TLC%20expertise.aspx</a></font></span></p><p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\"><br/><br/></font></p>"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "The TICAL meetings are intended to provide a regular forum where Inland Revenue can meet with representatives of external bodies who have relevant expertise, experience and interest - initially Chartered Accountants Australia and New Zealand, New Zealand Law Society, and the Corporate Taxpayers Group, with a view to discussing important legal and or technical issues that have arisen or are anticipated. The matters discussed will be of a general rather than a taxpayer-specific nature. Issues can be put forward for discussion by Inland Revenue or any of the external bodies."@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "OCTC content plan"@en ;
