<http://smartlogic.com/term#218546902444358781860379535583399>
        rdf:type          <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Legally-defined-term> , <http://smartlogic.com/class#Information> ;
        <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#LegalDefinition>
                "A document provided for which all of the following are true: the document is issued because the price of supply has increased after a tax invoice has been issued; the document contains all relevant information required to be provided in the document under the Goods and Services Tax Act 1985 and includes a document deemed to be a debit note under s 25(3A) of the Goods and Services Tax Act 1985."@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfLegalDefinition>
                "Goods and Services Tax Act, ss 2 and 25  (Reprint as at 2 June 2016)"@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Is-defined-by>
                <http://smartlogic.com/term#769477633007581059603718679399876> ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "Business Rules business terms"@en ;
        sem:guid          "9c3b99a2-5943-5eec-802d-d1089ca075cc" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#IRFinancialInformation> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://smartlogic.com/label#218546902444358781860379535583399_English> .

<http://smartlogic.com/term#219099017746331729706696572193112>
        rdf:type          <http://smartlogic.com/class#Obligation> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#HasRelatedIRForm>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#AnnualMaoriAuthorityCreditAccountReturnIncludingFDP-foreignDividendPayment-AccountReturn> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#FDP-foreignDividendPayment-AccountReturn> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#FDP-foreignDividendPayment-AccountReturn-MaoriAuthorities> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#HasType>
                <http://smartlogic.com/term#332232282734990593924592237114874> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#LastReviewedDate>
                "2017-04-03"^^xsd:date ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition>
                "General - START Help"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition0>
                "Concept model glossary"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "FDP was a type of income tax a New Zealand company may have been liable to pay on passive income it derived in the form of dividends received from outside New Zealand. This term replaced foreign dividend withholding payment (FDWP). An FDP account was a memorandum account that a company could maintain, in which it recorded any FDP credits and debits (if a company did not choose to maintain an FDP account, it recorded these entries in its ICA). The entries and rules for FDP accounts were largely the same as those for an ICA. This term replaced \"withholding payment account (WPA)\". An FDP credit was the type of tax credit a company recorded in its ICA (or its FDP account, if it held one) when the company paid FDP tax. FDP credits could be attached to dividends in the same manner as imputation credits. "@en ;
