        skos:broader      <http://example.com/IRD-test-model#Job-title> ;
        skos:definition   "The Solicitor-General is the second law officer of state in New Zealand, behind the Attorney-General. The Solicitor-General is also the chief executive of the Crown Law Office, that comprises lawyers employed to represent the Attorney-General in court proceedings in New Zealand. In practice, the Solicitor-General provides advice directly to Ministers, departments and agencies of government and will appear as Senior Counsel for government interests in litigation and in particular appellate court matters. A key responsibility is to advise the government on constitutional questions."@en ;
