        skos:definition     "Data, information and knowledge management embraces all the generic concepts of management, including the planning, organizing, structuring, processing, controlling, evaluation and reporting of information activities, all of which is needed in order to meet the needs of those with organisational roles or functions that depend on data, information or knowledge. These generic concepts allow it to be presented to the audience or the correct group of people."@en ;
