                "<p>IR website; </p><p>Corporate Finance content</p>"@en ;
        sem:guid          "968b05a4-aa5e-55ca-b233-5918ac96dcf0" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#ExtraPay> , <http://smartlogic.com/term#133464950737212625130954948425202> ;
        skos:definition   "<p>A redundancy payment is a sum of money paid to an employee when their position becomes redundant—meaning the role is no longer required by the employer due to restructuring, downsizing, or other genuine business reasons.<br><br>Redundancy payments are taxed at the lump sum rate, which is based on the employee’s estimated annual income including the redundancy amount.&nbsp;This means the payment is taxed at the employee’s top marginal tax rate for the year.<br></p>"@en ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://smartlogic.com/label#516424298372848718940092677055248_English> .

