                true ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "Schedular payments (formerly known as withholding payments) are made to people who are not employees but who are employed under a contract for services. Generally the relationship of the parties is not strictly one of employer and employee. Refer START Help: Schedular payments."@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "Concept Model Glossary; Business Rules business terms"@en ;
        <http://smartlogic.com/relationship#Previously-known-as_4_None_None>
                <http://smartlogic.com/label#35049154096265754693837_English_2829> ;
        sem:guid          "5a8f34b8-682a-5e66-92a9-9ac05bc4204d" ;
        skos:broader      <http://smartlogic.com/term#133464950737212625130954948425202> ;
        skos:definition   "A schedular payment is when you’re paid as a contractor and some tax is taken out before you get paid, similar to PAYE, but you’re still self‑employed. This may be a contractor or entity such as a partnership who performs activities outlined in Schedule 4 of the Income Tax Act 2007. This kind of payment is subject to tax at a flat rate."@en ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/Cleaned-Inland-Revenue-model#Directors-Fees> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#CertificateOfExemption> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://smartlogic.com/label#547761871254757204639149044657826_English> .

