        sem:guid          "e248d359-f083-5732-ac9a-024e72b503f3" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/IRD-test-model#Job-title> ;
        skos:definition   "The New Zealand Government Chief Digital Officer (GCDO) is responsible for leading digital transformation across the public service. The GCDO's role includes setting digital policy and standards, improving digital investments, establishing and managing digital services, and ensuring system-wide digital assurance. "@en ;
        skos:historyNote  "On 1 April 2026, the Government Digital Delivery Agency was established. The Government Digital Delivery Agency (GDDA) is part of the Public Service Commission (PSC) and takes on the functions of the Government Chief Digital Office (GCDO). The GDDA brings together system leadership, delivery support and capability functions to support digital public services across government."@en ;
        skos:related      <http://example.com/IRD-test-model#Government-Chief-Information-Office> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#GovernmentDigitalDeliveryAgency> , <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#GovernmentOfNewZealand> ;
