<http://smartlogic.com/term#616011861049696073175>
        rdf:type          <http://smartlogic.com/class#Party-classification> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#HasRelatedIRForm>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#IRDNumberApplication-Non-resident-offshoreIndividual> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#HasRelatedInformation>
                <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#IRDNumberApplication-CustomerDueDiligence> ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Instance>
                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition>
                "General - START Help"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "<p>This definition applies to IRD number applications. A separate definition of 'offshore person' applies for Residential Land Withholding Tax (RLWT) purposes.<br/>Individual - An offshore individual is someone who: is a New Zealand citizen and has been overseas for the last three or more years continuously (and is not currently in New Zealand); or doesn’t have a New Zealand residence class visa granted by Immigration New Zealand (can be in NZ or out of NZ); or has a New Zealand residence class visa granted by Immigration New Zealand and has been overseas for the last twelve or more months continuously (and is not currently in New Zealand). A customer with NZ residency who is present in NZ is not considered an offshore person. Customers entering NZ with an Australian passport are automatically granted residency. This is sometimes electronic and so there will be no evidence provided to Inland Revenue to confirm this. They will not be considered an offshore person unless they meet the criteria from the third point above.<br/>Examples: 1) Kelly is a New Zealand citizen by birth and left New Zealand in 2005 to work in Germany. She has been out of New Zealand continuously since 2005. Kelly will start working in New Zealand shortly and wants to apply for an IRD number before she arrives. The application form Kelly will use is an IR742 as she will still meet the definition of an &#34;offshore person&#34;. 2) Yuka normally lives in Japan and is now in New Zealand on a working visa. As a working visa is not considered to be a residence class visa Yuka will complete an IR742 to apply for an IRD number. 3) Alice has a NZ residence class visa and has lived in the Netherlands continuously for the last thirteen months. Alice is planning to purchase a house in New Zealand while still living overseas. The form that she will need to complete is an IR742 as she is considered to be an &#34;offshore person&#34;.<br/>Specific visas – customers on these visas will be considered offshore persons: Student visa; Working Holiday Scheme (WHS) work visa; Temporary work visa. Company - A company is an offshore person if it is: incorporated outside New Zealand, or 25% or more owned or controlled by offshore persons. Trust - A trust will be an offshore person if: 25% or more of its governing body are offshore; or offshore person(s) have 25% or more beneficial interest or entitlement to its trust property; or 25% or more of persons with the right to amend or control the trust’s trust deed are offshore persons; or 25% or more of persons with the right to control the composition of the trust’s governing body are offshore persons. Unit trust - A unit trust will be an offshore person if: the manager or trustee (or both) are offshore person(s); or offshore person(s) have beneficial interest or 25% or more of the trust''s property. Non-individual partnership, unincorporated joint venture, or other unincorporated body - A non-individual partnership, unincorporated joint venture, or other unincorporated body will be an offshore person if: 25% or more of its partners (or members) are offshore persons; or offshore person(s) have a beneficial interest or entitlement to 25% or more of its profits or assets; or offshore person(s) have the right to exercise (or control the exercise) of 25% or more of voting power at a meeting.<br/></p>"@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Source-of-term>
                "TIB; Website glossary"@en ;
        sem:guid          "e6cc7e17-3cb9-5bb3-b487-4f1f241b3159" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#OffshoreStatus> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://smartlogic.com/label#616011861049696073175_English> .

