                false ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition>
                "General - START Help"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "When a company is in financial difficulties, a receiver can be appointed to oversee its financial management. This can happen either at the request of the company management and/or shareholders, or if a creditor the company successfully applies to have the company put into receivership. If there is a reasonable possibility that the company can trade its way out of its difficulties then the receiver may attempt to do this. In other situations the receiver may oversee the winding-up of the company."@en ;
        sem:guid          "8c7d33ae-731b-5672-8d90-9c51ed371cb1" ;
        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#Insolvency> ;
        skosxl:prefLabel  <http://smartlogic.com/label#83752631923000545524903_English> .

