        skos:broader      <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#ReserveSchemes0> ;
        skos:definition   "The income equalisation scheme allows taxpayers to deposit income from farming, fishing or forestry with Inland Revenue. The money is paid into a special account and earns interest at 3% per annum on amounts left on deposit for more than 12 months. The interest paid becomes part of the deposit for tax purposes."@en ;
