        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel#SourceOfDefinition>
                "<p>TCO Corporate Space intranet page<br/></p><p><span lang=\"mi-NZ\"><a href=\"https://irnz.sharepoint.com/sites/CORP-tax-counsel-office/SitePages/What-we-do.aspx\">https://irnz.sharepoint.com/sites/CORP-tax-counsel-office/SitePages/What-we-do.aspx</a></span></p><p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\"><br/><br/></font></p>"@en ;
        <http://example.com/InlandRevenueModel-current-#BusinessDefinition>
                "The disputes review service conducts adjudication reviews (a part of the tax dispute resolution process.) This process was designed so that tax disputes could be resolved at an early stage to reduce the number of litigated cases. Our role is to take a fresh look at disputes in an impartial and independent manner and provide technically accurate decisions. ​​​​​​​The adjudication process is independent of the Commissioner's investigative or audit function. A detailed adjudication report is provided to the taxpayer and the CCS staff involved, explaining the decision in relation to the proposed adjustments and detailed analysis of how the decision was reached."@en ;
        <http://example.com/NZ-IRD#Evidence>
